A||||10||Dave85||Sunroof?||||1||
Z||000000||Dave85||12-14-1999||06:22 PM||||<BR>I know I've read somewhere on here about replaceing the rubber/ plastic washers. I went to Pontiac and all they show is the bolts and 2 washers.  My question is: do the bolts come with some sort of washer attatched. Mine are leaking from the latch bolts. And guess what---- they are $5.00 each. The rubber/plastic washers are $2.50 each. It's looking like $25.00 to re-do the glass.  Is this correct?<BR>       Dave||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-14-1999||06:47 PM||||if the hardware is good, but only the seals are shot try a 10 speed innertube (26x1.25 27x1.25 are common size ones.) that tube is pretty thin and cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||12-14-1999||07:01 PM||||This is similar to another situation I ran across. Copper washers are 89 cents each, but a penny with a hole drilled in it, is fairly cheap.  ||||reg||12
Z||000003||Dave85||12-14-1999||07:49 PM||||Great ideas!! I had thought of dipping the tops of the bolts in plasticoat.  THANKS<P>Dave||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:17 PM||||Don't use anything metal as it will scratch the coating on the glass.  You could use parts of an innertube, but why not just spend the $25 and do it right.  Lots less hassle that way, although the innertube thing would be good for a temporary fix.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||12-14-1999||11:44 PM||||I fixed mine with some black rubber flat washers from Lowe's and some clear GE silicone. Put the rubber washer on each side of the hardware, fill the hole in the glass with the silicone, put the stuff together, but do not tighten it until the silicone sets up and that is it. Total costs- about $1.50||||reg||1
Z||000006||Carrolles||12-15-1999||06:26 AM||||I bought the washers/bolts from Pontiac and they worked great.  The bolts have an integral washer built in.||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||06:32 PM||||Carrolles,<P>What was the cost of those parts (GM#20424246 - tabs and #20362045 - bushings) from the dealership?  I am going to replace mine too and was wondering how much $.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||5
Z||000008||Dave85||12-15-1999||09:54 PM||||Yes that's the dealership price. $5.00 per bolt and $2.50 per washer!<BR>I didn't see how much the hinges were though.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-16-1999||01:47 AM||||I just replaced the front hinges and washers on mine.  $13US for both hinges and both plastic washers.  You have to replace the washers at the same time.  My washers came apart in about 37 pieces and you can't replace those (the right way) with anything else.  They are fitted to the hole and the bolt.  It's hard to explain, but just trust me on this.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Dave85||12-16-1999||10:27 AM||||Thanks for all the replies! I guess I'll shell out the $25.00 and fix it right. I've already spent $70.00 on the seal so what the heck.<BR>Thanks again, <BR>Dave||||reg||1
